WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.512 --> 00:00:01.571
- Good morning, BelieveNation.

00:00:01.571 --> 00:00:02.864
My name is Evan Carmichael.

00:00:02.864 --> 00:00:04.002
My one word is believe

00:00:04.002 --> 00:00:05.924
and I believe that
entrepreneurs will solve

00:00:05.924 --> 00:00:08.084
all of the world's major problems.

00:00:08.084 --> 00:00:09.744
So to help you on your journey,

00:00:09.744 --> 00:00:14.141
today's message is a lot of
people don't want success.

00:00:14.141 --> 00:00:16.327
Over to you, Maya Angelou.

00:00:16.327 --> 00:00:18.288
(rooster crowing)

00:00:18.288 --> 00:00:20.680
♫ I wake up every morning.

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:23.401
♫ Entspresso keep me going.

00:00:23.401 --> 00:00:26.984
♫ I wake up every morning.

00:00:28.437 --> 00:00:30.772
- Well, a lot of people
don't really want success.

00:00:30.772 --> 00:00:32.171
- [Interviewer] I've
never understood that.

00:00:32.171 --> 00:00:33.206
- This is true.

00:00:33.206 --> 00:00:34.981
- You mean because they don't want it

00:00:34.981 --> 00:00:36.604
and the best evidence of that is that--

00:00:36.604 --> 00:00:37.929
- They fail.
- They fail.

00:00:37.929 --> 00:00:39.612
And the best evidence of that
is they don't try things.

00:00:39.612 --> 00:00:42.033
- That's right, that's right.

00:00:42.033 --> 00:00:46.033
But to succeed means that
you're in front of God

00:00:46.916 --> 00:00:49.650
and lots of responsible people

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:53.817
and you have to either eat
your words or stand by them.

00:00:56.301 --> 00:01:00.468
I think that I have agreed a
long time ago, Charlie Rose,

00:01:02.051 --> 00:01:04.801
this may be my greatest blessing.

00:01:06.107 --> 00:01:09.524
I agreed a long time ago that I will die.

00:01:11.251 --> 00:01:13.334
Now, if I can admit that,

00:01:15.766 --> 00:01:19.012
that no matter what happens,
I will do this thing,

00:01:19.012 --> 00:01:21.572
this is the biggest bugaboo of them all.

00:01:21.572 --> 00:01:23.771
I will do that, well then,

00:01:23.771 --> 00:01:27.104
why couldn't I attempt something lesser?

00:01:28.614 --> 00:01:30.071
So I will try.

00:01:30.071 --> 00:01:32.864
- Your fear of failure
has done more to harm you

00:01:32.864 --> 00:01:35.702
than any insult anyone has thrown at you.

00:01:35.702 --> 00:01:37.961
Your fear of failure has
done more to harm you

00:01:37.961 --> 00:01:41.181
than any beatings that
anybody's ever put on you.

00:01:41.181 --> 00:01:43.469
Your fear of failure is the biggest thing

00:01:43.469 --> 00:01:45.826
that's holding you back from
achieving amazing things

00:01:45.826 --> 00:01:48.053
and building amazing companies.

00:01:48.053 --> 00:01:50.368
And the biggest failure of all

00:01:50.368 --> 00:01:52.838
is not doing the thing
that you want to do.

00:01:52.838 --> 00:01:55.045
Not doing the thing that is inside you.

00:01:55.045 --> 00:01:58.809
That you know if you did
it, it's going to be amazing

00:01:58.809 --> 00:02:00.889
but there's this huge wall of fear

00:02:00.889 --> 00:02:02.522
that you have to break though.

00:02:02.522 --> 00:02:04.836
And I think we need to have
a discussion around fear.

00:02:04.836 --> 00:02:07.626
I think we see fear as the
negative, fear as the enemy.

00:02:07.626 --> 00:02:10.696
You know, we shouldn't do
anything that we're afraid of.

00:02:10.696 --> 00:02:12.913
But if you look at all the
people that you look up to,

00:02:12.913 --> 00:02:14.617
all the people that you respect,

00:02:14.617 --> 00:02:16.670
athletes, entrepreneurs, musicians,

00:02:16.670 --> 00:02:18.745
whoever it is that you look up to,

00:02:18.745 --> 00:02:21.264
they had an insane amount of fear

00:02:21.264 --> 00:02:23.903
to get to where they wanted to go.

00:02:23.903 --> 00:02:25.285
There's that great diagram,

00:02:25.285 --> 00:02:27.929
I've got a t-shirt I made
about the comfort zone,

00:02:27.929 --> 00:02:30.239
where it shows where your comfort zone is

00:02:30.239 --> 00:02:32.378
and it shows where the magic happens

00:02:32.378 --> 00:02:34.802
and the magic always happens
outside your comfort zone.

00:02:34.802 --> 00:02:37.056
And the more you can stretch
and the more you can push

00:02:37.056 --> 00:02:40.019
what makes you scared, then
the more you'll be able

00:02:40.019 --> 00:02:42.984
to create for yourself,
for your community,

00:02:42.984 --> 00:02:45.015
for your family, for the world.

00:02:45.015 --> 00:02:46.918
If you just stay within this bubble

00:02:46.918 --> 00:02:48.969
and you never do the thing
that you're afraid of,

00:02:48.969 --> 00:02:50.479
you're never going to grow

00:02:50.479 --> 00:02:52.542
and you're never really going to be happy

00:02:52.542 --> 00:02:54.135
and at the end of your life
you're going to look back

00:02:54.135 --> 00:02:57.004
and be filled with regret
that you didn't do this thing.

00:02:57.004 --> 00:02:58.412
There's been a lot of times that,

00:02:58.412 --> 00:03:00.308
at least for me, I'm sure you can relate,

00:03:00.308 --> 00:03:02.597
there's something I was so afraid to do,

00:03:02.597 --> 00:03:04.139
I was so afraid to do it and then,

00:03:04.139 --> 00:03:06.216
once I did it, I was
like, hey you know what,

00:03:06.216 --> 00:03:07.786
that actually wasn't that bad.

00:03:07.786 --> 00:03:09.237
And then you do it over
and over and over again

00:03:09.237 --> 00:03:10.964
and the fear is totally gone.

00:03:10.964 --> 00:03:12.866
I think about making videos on YouTube.

00:03:12.866 --> 00:03:16.302
The first time I got in
front of a YouTube camera,

00:03:16.302 --> 00:03:20.320
I had to have my sister or
somebody on my team come in,

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:23.676
I used my own camera, focus it,

00:03:23.676 --> 00:03:26.178
and then leave the room
'cause I was too afraid

00:03:26.178 --> 00:03:27.894
of their judgments, of their opinions,

00:03:27.894 --> 00:03:29.704
even though they didn't really care.

00:03:29.704 --> 00:03:31.486
They were actually supportive of me,

00:03:31.486 --> 00:03:34.287
but I was just too afraid to
talk in front of somebody else.

00:03:34.287 --> 00:03:36.418
When I was walking on the street

00:03:36.418 --> 00:03:38.266
and filming myself, I'd be too afraid

00:03:38.266 --> 00:03:41.124
of other people, their judgments,

00:03:41.124 --> 00:03:44.282
their looking, and it throwing me off.

00:03:44.282 --> 00:03:46.488
And so if I let that prevent me

00:03:46.488 --> 00:03:48.235
from actually making videos,

00:03:48.235 --> 00:03:50.083
then I wouldn't have made this

00:03:50.083 --> 00:03:51.847
and I wouldn't be helping you guys.

00:03:51.847 --> 00:03:53.262
You wouldn't have anything to watch

00:03:53.262 --> 00:03:55.253
from me on a regular basis.

00:03:55.253 --> 00:03:58.691
Right, I wouldn't have closing
in on 800,000 subscribers.

00:03:58.691 --> 00:04:00.353
It wouldn't be happening.

00:04:00.353 --> 00:04:02.410
And that would be a huge hole for me,

00:04:02.410 --> 00:04:04.200
that would make me feel really bad.

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:06.517
Fast forward to age 90,
looking back on my life,

00:04:06.517 --> 00:04:08.340
say I didn't do that because I was afraid

00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:10.304
of getting in front of a
camera and saying something?

00:04:10.304 --> 00:04:12.710
For me, that's how I'd get
through the immediate fear,

00:04:12.710 --> 00:04:15.436
is I'd fast forward to the end of my life

00:04:15.436 --> 00:04:18.293
and I'd trade off this
immediate tiny little fear

00:04:18.293 --> 00:04:21.210
of getting up in front of a
camera and doing something

00:04:21.210 --> 00:04:24.149
versus an entire lifetime of regret

00:04:24.149 --> 00:04:26.810
and that's what I want to try to avoid.

00:04:26.810 --> 00:04:28.721
And so failure is going to happen.

00:04:28.721 --> 00:04:30.775
Failure is going to happen, you will fail.

00:04:30.775 --> 00:04:32.638
The most successful
people in the world fail,

00:04:32.638 --> 00:04:34.427
over and over and over
and over and over again.

00:04:34.427 --> 00:04:36.922
They fail, they fail their way to success.

00:04:36.922 --> 00:04:38.549
Everybody has had massive failures.

00:04:38.549 --> 00:04:40.097
If you don't have any failures,

00:04:40.097 --> 00:04:42.312
it means you haven't tried anything.

00:04:42.312 --> 00:04:43.975
And so don't be afraid of failures.

00:04:43.975 --> 00:04:46.232
I just try to make
failures on a small scale.

00:04:46.232 --> 00:04:47.646
A lot of the videos that we've made

00:04:47.646 --> 00:04:49.467
for this YouTube channel
don't go anywhere.

00:04:49.467 --> 00:04:51.918
Series die all the time.

00:04:51.918 --> 00:04:54.800
The top 10 was just one
that I did as a one off

00:04:54.800 --> 00:04:57.139
and it did well so I just did
it again, let's do it again,

00:04:57.139 --> 00:04:59.032
let's do it twice a week
then three times a week,

00:04:59.032 --> 00:05:00.685
five times a week and it builds,

00:05:00.685 --> 00:05:03.065
and others, I don't even remember
how many we've killed off.

00:05:03.065 --> 00:05:04.898
I'm not held up by it.

00:05:06.723 --> 00:05:08.319
It's just part of the distant past.

00:05:08.319 --> 00:05:10.342
I don't remember the names
of the series anymore.

00:05:10.342 --> 00:05:12.669
I loved them when I launched them

00:05:12.669 --> 00:05:16.079
and you guys didn't relate to
them as well so we killed it.

00:05:16.079 --> 00:05:18.487
And I expect most things to fail.

00:05:18.487 --> 00:05:19.792
That's okay.

00:05:19.792 --> 00:05:24.122
I don't tie my self worth
to one idea working out.

00:05:24.122 --> 00:05:26.091
Because if you can do that,

00:05:26.091 --> 00:05:29.005
if you can get past the fear of failure

00:05:29.005 --> 00:05:32.366
and just expect things not
to work at the beginning.

00:05:32.366 --> 00:05:34.462
And just keep driving and keep improving,

00:05:34.462 --> 00:05:35.517
keep getting better.

00:05:35.517 --> 00:05:37.900
Like nothing that you try
at the beginning works.

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:41.527
Everything you do will
fail at the beginning.

00:05:41.527 --> 00:05:43.305
Any skill that you try to learn,

00:05:43.305 --> 00:05:45.303
you're going to suck at it
at the start and it's normal.

00:05:45.303 --> 00:05:46.703
If you're trying to learn a language

00:05:46.703 --> 00:05:48.654
or pick up a new skill or
you're going to go snowboarding

00:05:48.654 --> 00:05:51.394
or mountain biking or learn
how to do YouTube or lights

00:05:51.394 --> 00:05:54.337
or whatever it is, you're going
to suck at it at the start.

00:05:54.337 --> 00:05:57.257
That's okay, that's normal.

00:05:57.257 --> 00:05:59.528
Expect it, embrace it.

00:05:59.528 --> 00:06:01.381
And know you're going to continue to fail

00:06:01.381 --> 00:06:02.534
and not get so caught up

00:06:02.534 --> 00:06:05.417
on every failure damaging
your psyche so much.

00:06:05.417 --> 00:06:07.501
And then at the other end,

00:06:07.501 --> 00:06:09.880
and this is where
modeled success can help,

00:06:09.880 --> 00:06:12.219
by looking at these people and knowing

00:06:12.219 --> 00:06:15.088
that they made it through,
so if you stick with it

00:06:15.088 --> 00:06:17.839
and you embrace the
failure and you keep going

00:06:17.839 --> 00:06:20.312
and you keep working and you keep hustling

00:06:20.312 --> 00:06:22.568
that eventually you'll make it through,

00:06:22.568 --> 00:06:25.630
just like they did, but if you quit,

00:06:25.630 --> 00:06:28.310
and you stop and you hold yourself back

00:06:28.310 --> 00:06:31.248
because you're afraid, then
you're going to continue

00:06:31.248 --> 00:06:33.965
to live a life that you're going to regret

00:06:33.965 --> 00:06:36.822
instead of doing the thing
that you were going to do.

00:06:36.822 --> 00:06:38.103
So the question of the day today is,

00:06:38.103 --> 00:06:39.394
I'm curious, what is the thing

00:06:39.394 --> 00:06:42.425
that you are most afraid of right now?

00:06:42.425 --> 00:06:44.696
Leave it down in the comments below.

00:06:44.696 --> 00:06:46.237
Really curious to find out.

00:06:46.237 --> 00:06:48.479
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Rebecca Zhou.

00:06:48.479 --> 00:06:50.301
Rebecca, thank you so much for picking up

00:06:50.301 --> 00:06:52.043
a copy of my book Your One Word.

00:06:52.043 --> 00:06:53.769
I really appreciate your support

00:06:53.769 --> 00:06:55.745
and I hope you enjoyed the read.

00:06:55.745 --> 00:06:57.250
So thank you guys so much for watching.

00:06:57.250 --> 00:06:58.506
I believe in you.

00:06:58.506 --> 00:07:00.339
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:07:00.339 --> 00:07:02.112
and whatever your one word is.

00:07:02.112 --> 00:07:04.653
Much love and I'll see
you again tomorrow morning

00:07:04.653 --> 00:07:07.711
for another shot of Entspresso.

00:07:07.711 --> 00:07:09.991
♫ I wake up every morning.

00:07:09.991 --> 00:07:13.658
♫ Entspresso keep me going.

00:07:17.309 --> 00:07:20.659
- Socrates said practice death daily.

00:07:20.659 --> 00:07:23.835
He didn't mean that in a morbid sense.

00:07:23.835 --> 00:07:27.906
He meant that if we
really consciously realize

00:07:27.906 --> 00:07:31.850
and remember everyday that
we're all going to die,

00:07:31.850 --> 00:07:34.760
then we live life differently

00:07:34.760 --> 00:07:37.905
because, first of all, we
don't sweat the small stuff

00:07:37.905 --> 00:07:42.082
and when it comes to death
everything is small stuff.

00:07:42.082 --> 00:07:45.680
It's the same thing
that the Romans thought.

00:07:45.680 --> 00:07:49.884
They would carve on
statues and on trees MM,

00:07:49.884 --> 00:07:52.301
memento mori, remember death.

00:07:52.301 --> 00:07:54.570
Again, it's one of the things...

00:07:54.570 --> 00:07:57.350
We actually have now a dedicated reporter

00:07:57.350 --> 00:08:00.828
on the Huffington Post covering death,

00:08:00.828 --> 00:08:04.881
because again, that's a
huge silence in our culture.

00:08:04.881 --> 00:08:07.677
That the thing that is the
absolutely inevitable part

00:08:07.677 --> 00:08:10.541
of our lives is not being
covered by our media.

00:08:10.541 --> 00:08:12.661
The Columbia Journalism Review,

00:08:12.661 --> 00:08:14.294
his first name is Jaweed.

00:08:14.294 --> 00:08:15.857
If you can't remember his last name,

00:08:15.857 --> 00:08:18.418
he's doing amazing things around death,

00:08:18.418 --> 00:08:20.050
in our religion section,

00:08:20.050 --> 00:08:22.307
which is next to our science section

00:08:22.307 --> 00:08:24.626
because increasingly we're trying to see

00:08:24.626 --> 00:08:26.861
how the two are not opposed to each other.

00:08:26.861 --> 00:08:29.785
Dogmas may be opposed, but
the heart of every religion

00:08:29.785 --> 00:08:31.880
is very connected to the heart

00:08:31.880 --> 00:08:34.533
of huge scientific discoveries.

00:08:34.533 --> 00:08:37.783
So my point to go back to death is that

00:08:39.350 --> 00:08:41.386
if we make it part of life,

00:08:41.386 --> 00:08:43.720
if we make us lead life differently,

00:08:43.720 --> 00:08:46.896
so when the time comes for us to die,

00:08:46.896 --> 00:08:49.287
we will be prepared for it.

00:08:49.287 --> 00:08:50.932
- Because we practiced it.

00:08:50.932 --> 00:08:53.245
- Because we'll have
practiced it, every day.

00:08:53.245 --> 00:08:55.667
- I tell people all the time,

00:08:55.667 --> 00:08:57.570
and I really believe this,

00:08:57.570 --> 00:09:01.664
that I exist to show
people what's possible.

00:09:01.664 --> 00:09:02.863
I really do.

00:09:02.863 --> 00:09:05.662
It's like go for it, try it,

00:09:05.662 --> 00:09:08.150
because another thing, I am no different

00:09:08.150 --> 00:09:10.240
than anyone else out there.

00:09:10.240 --> 00:09:13.053
I am not here to say I have a superpower

00:09:13.053 --> 00:09:16.720
and it was all this,
it was just try it, go.

00:09:17.725 --> 00:09:20.121
Let's see what happens.

00:09:20.121 --> 00:09:23.535
And all of a sudden when
you get rid of judgment,

00:09:23.535 --> 00:09:25.229
now you can be creative,

00:09:25.229 --> 00:09:27.639
but any bit of judgment kills creativity.

00:09:27.639 --> 00:09:30.143
Anytime you start to go,
well, maybe I shouldn't.

00:09:30.143 --> 00:09:32.199
And it's funny because you look at lipsync

00:09:32.199 --> 00:09:35.163
or you look at any kind of
dancing or anything like that,

00:09:35.163 --> 00:09:38.580
as soon as people see you
being inhibited, you're done.

00:09:38.580 --> 00:09:40.590
You're like oh, this guy, what is this.

00:09:40.590 --> 00:09:44.751
But all they want is for
you to give all you got.

00:09:44.751 --> 00:09:46.113
- [Interviewer] Just put it out there.

00:09:46.113 --> 00:09:47.458
- And then everybody's with you,

00:09:47.458 --> 00:09:52.177
and let me tell you, Terry
Crews is going to give you 150%

00:09:52.177 --> 00:09:55.233
no matter what and I learned
that's my whole career.

00:09:55.233 --> 00:09:57.400
- You should just observe.

00:09:58.610 --> 00:10:01.740
If everybody makes a little effort,

00:10:01.740 --> 00:10:05.710
everybody take a little time
for this piece of life, okay?

00:10:05.710 --> 00:10:09.069
Not for your family, not for your carrier,

00:10:09.069 --> 00:10:11.466
not for something else, something else.

00:10:11.466 --> 00:10:13.887
Just for this piece of life.

00:10:13.887 --> 00:10:16.099
Give it little time because
this is the most important

00:10:16.099 --> 00:10:18.672
piece of life in your life, isn't it?

00:10:18.672 --> 00:10:19.612
Yes or no?

00:10:19.612 --> 00:10:20.445
- Yes.

00:10:21.390 --> 00:10:22.917
- Even if you're in love with somebody,

00:10:22.917 --> 00:10:25.551
still this is the most important
piece of life, isn't it?

00:10:25.551 --> 00:10:28.250
So pay some attention to this.

00:10:28.250 --> 00:10:29.835
How does it happen?

00:10:29.835 --> 00:10:31.781
Why have you taken it for granted?

00:10:31.781 --> 00:10:34.261
Believe me, you're not
going to be here forever.

00:10:34.261 --> 00:10:35.977
I'll bless you with a long life,

00:10:35.977 --> 00:10:38.395
but you're going to fall dead one day.

00:10:38.395 --> 00:10:39.864
Yes or no?

00:10:39.864 --> 00:10:41.876
- [Woman] Yes
- [Audience] Yes

00:10:41.876 --> 00:10:44.012
- So do not take this for granted.

00:10:44.012 --> 00:10:45.613
If you wake up in the morning,

00:10:45.613 --> 00:10:48.863
tomorrow if you wake up in the morning.

00:10:51.180 --> 00:10:54.264
It's not my wish, but I want you to know,

00:10:54.264 --> 00:10:57.026
of all the people who go to bed tonight,

00:10:57.026 --> 00:11:01.193
over a million people will
not wake up tomorrow morning.

00:11:02.250 --> 00:11:05.772
And tomorrow, if you and me
wake up tomorrow morning,

00:11:05.772 --> 00:11:08.734
is it not a fantastic thing?

00:11:08.734 --> 00:11:10.531
A million people did not wake up.

00:11:10.531 --> 00:11:11.581
You woke up.

00:11:11.581 --> 00:11:13.863
Is it not a great thing?

00:11:13.863 --> 00:11:16.500
Just look at the ceiling and smile.

00:11:16.500 --> 00:11:17.485
(audience applause)

00:11:17.485 --> 00:11:18.513
You are still awake!

00:11:18.513 --> 00:11:20.109
You're still there!

00:11:20.109 --> 00:11:23.276
And for many, many millions of people,

00:11:24.722 --> 00:11:28.255
somebody who is dear to
them did not wake up.

00:11:28.255 --> 00:11:31.276
So just check those five,
six people around you,

00:11:31.276 --> 00:11:32.586
they all woke up?

00:11:32.586 --> 00:11:35.050
Wow, it's a fantastic day!

00:11:35.050 --> 00:11:37.925
You woke up and everybody who matters

00:11:37.925 --> 00:11:40.858
to you around you woke up.

00:11:40.858 --> 00:11:42.763
Is it not fantastic day?

00:11:42.763 --> 00:11:44.710
You don't think so?

00:11:44.710 --> 00:11:46.685
- Yes (laughs)

00:11:46.685 --> 00:11:47.921
(audience laughter)

00:11:47.921 --> 00:11:49.266
- You don't seem to think so.

00:11:49.266 --> 00:11:50.366
- [Woman] Yes.

00:11:50.366 --> 00:11:52.068
- Because the problem is just this,

00:11:52.068 --> 00:11:56.160
you are living with an
idea that you're immortal.

00:11:56.160 --> 00:11:57.863
When I say you're immortal,

00:11:57.863 --> 00:12:00.309
you're not actually
thinking you're immortal,

00:12:00.309 --> 00:12:03.645
but you are not conscious
of your mortality.

00:12:03.645 --> 00:12:06.092
If you are not conscious
of your mortality,

00:12:06.092 --> 00:12:08.840
somewhere you think
you're immortal, isn't it?

00:12:08.840 --> 00:12:10.416
How many moments in a day

00:12:10.416 --> 00:12:13.600
are you conscious that you're mortal?

00:12:13.600 --> 00:12:17.365
If you are conscious, would
you have time to crimp?

00:12:17.365 --> 00:12:20.008
Would you have time to
fight with somebody?

00:12:20.008 --> 00:12:23.443
Would you have time to do
some rubbish with your life

00:12:23.443 --> 00:12:26.967
if you knew, if you are
conscious that you're mortal,

00:12:26.967 --> 00:12:30.895
you will do nothing other
than what is absolutely needed

00:12:30.895 --> 00:12:33.501
for you and everybody around you.

00:12:33.501 --> 00:12:35.115
This one thing, if you do,

00:12:35.115 --> 00:12:37.137
if you just remind yourself.

00:12:37.137 --> 00:12:38.721
Don't think it's a negative thing.

00:12:38.721 --> 00:12:40.050
Death is not a negative thing.

00:12:40.050 --> 00:12:42.690
It's the only thing which
has added value to life.

00:12:42.690 --> 00:12:45.749
If you're here forever,
you'd be unbearable.

00:12:45.749 --> 00:12:49.180
(audience laughter)
- (laughs) Yes, yes.

00:12:49.180 --> 00:12:52.513
- Aren't we glad everybody dies one day?

00:12:54.054 --> 00:12:57.720
If you just become
conscious of this one thing,

00:12:57.720 --> 00:13:00.505
that always you're
conscious that I'm mortal,

00:13:00.505 --> 00:13:02.357
you don't have to think I will die today,

00:13:02.357 --> 00:13:04.277
we don't intend, we want
to live as far as possible,

00:13:04.277 --> 00:13:07.038
just you'll know, one day I will die.

00:13:07.038 --> 00:13:09.408
If you're just conscious
of this one thing,

00:13:09.408 --> 00:13:11.443
you will naturally become spiritual,

00:13:11.443 --> 00:13:13.620
every day, every moment,
if you remind yourself,

00:13:13.620 --> 00:13:16.135
this is a brief life, I am mortal,

00:13:16.135 --> 00:13:17.987
one day I will end.

00:13:17.987 --> 00:13:20.294
Just do this for two days and see.

00:13:20.294 --> 00:13:22.526
You'll become something truly fantastic

00:13:22.526 --> 00:13:24.218
within yourself, just this is all.

00:13:24.218 --> 00:13:25.995
- That is simply beautiful.

00:13:25.995 --> 00:13:28.135
- That's all that's needed.

00:13:28.135 --> 00:13:31.505
If you want to know the value of life,

00:13:31.505 --> 00:13:34.273
just know that it's a brief happening.

